 "prose": "Tuesday, October 20, was your weak day. You rang up $743 from 83 payments. A typical Tuesday is $1,115, so that was 33.4% below. Street and sidewalk permits near you may explain it. Three sidewalk and utility permits at 3021 Holmes Ave S, 292 feet away, cover that date, and so does a Comcast utility permit at 3001 Hennepin Ave, 406 feet away. A permit date is when the city wrote it down, not the day the street was closed. The whole week at Mosaic Coffee Co. was $8,873, down 2.0% from $9,057 the week before. Saturday ran 11.2% above typical.\n\nYour landlord's building at 3040 Hennepin Ave is now valued by the county at $3,200,000. That was $3,050,000, a rise of 4.9%. The tax bill is $101,001.94. A triple-net lease passes that on to you. Notices come in March. A Tax Court petition has to be filed by April 30 of the year the tax is paid.\n\nTwo doors down, at 3024 Hennepin Ave, Amazing Thailand has a pending on-sale liquor licence, 212 feet away. The Tasting Room, on your block at 1434 31st St W, got an approved wine licence on July 24. Curioso (406 feet) has wine, and Arizona Taco Company (406 feet) has liquor. All of them sell to people who might otherwise buy from you.\n\nAcross the street at 3045 Hennepin Ave, 282 feet away, a 228-unit, 5-story apartment building has a permit issued August 12. That means more people living and walking nearby in time.\n\nNearby sales, nearest first. 3045 Hennepin Ave sold for $3,000,000 in February 2026, but the deed is marked as left out of the county's price studies. 3018 Hennepin Ave sold for $1,100,000 in March 2025 with a plain warranty deed. 2908 Humboldt Ave S sold for $800,000 in July 2025, also a plain warranty deed. 1103 Lake St W sold for $1,683,182 in June 2026 on a non-standard deed. 2828 Hennepin Ave sold for $4,250,000 in April 2025, and that price covers more than one parcel.",
